.TH SISTA-C-API 3 "" "Sista" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
sista-c-api \- C interface to the Sista library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sista/api.h>
.PP
.B cc \-c program.c
.B c++ program.o \-lSista_api \-lSista
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The C API exposes Sista objects through opaque handle types such as
.BR FieldHandler_t ,
.BR PawnHandler_t ,
and
.BR ANSISettingsHandler_t .
Creation functions return a handle, and matching destruction functions
release resources owned by that handle.
.PP
Functions that perform an operation return a value from
.BR enum\ sista_ErrorCode .
.B SISTA_OK
indicates success.
After a failure,
.B sista_getLastErrorCode()
and
.B sista_getLastErrorMessage()
provide diagnostic information.
.PP
The installed
.B <sista/api.h>
header is authoritative for ownership rules and individual declarations.
In particular, consult the declaration of each pawn-creation function to see
whether the returned pawn remains owned by its field.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <sista/api.h>

int main(void)
{
    FieldHandler_t field = sista_createField(20, 8);
    if (field == NULL) {
        fprintf(stderr, "%s\en", sista_getLastErrorMessage());
        return 1;
    }

    if (sista_printField(field, '#') != SISTA_OK) {
        fprintf(stderr, "%s\en", sista_getLastErrorMessage());
        sista_destroyField(field);
        return 1;
    }

    return sista_destroyField(field) == SISTA_OK ? 0 : 1;
}
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Error information is intended to describe the most recent C API failure.
Callers should consume it immediately after the failing call and should not
assume that one thread's error state describes another thread's operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sista (3),
.BR sista-ansi (3),
.BR sista-field (3)
